# Regna (Chess Evolved) — project rules for agents

## Product vs engineering docs

- **Game design & vision:** `docs/regna.pdf` (GDD). Use it for _what_ we build (cards, chess evolution, modes), not for stack details.
- **Visual / art direction:** `docs/visual-charter.md` + `.cursor/rules/visual-design.mdc` (8-bit pixel + fluid motion; full-pixel UI). Update the charter when direction changes; client README for implementation notes.
- **Install & stack procedures:** `docs/regna-setup.md` (authoritative bootstrap).
- **Architecture / DB / ops decisions:** **`docs/TECHNICAL-LOG.md`** — append-only **global engineering log** (why the stack looks this way, dated decisions, rollout notes). **Not** a how-to or feature reference.
- **Package / area READMEs** — **how-to and reference** for what exists and how to use it. Put explanations here, not in rules, comments, or the technical log.

### README vs TECHNICAL-LOG (do not mix roles)

| Doc                                                | Role                                          | When to update                                                                                                     |
| -------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **`README.md`** (repo root)                        | Monorepo overview, quick start, links         | New package, root scripts, onboarding flow changes                                                                 |
| **`apps/*/README.md`**, **`packages/*/README.md`** | Scripts, env, layout, usage of that package   | New **usable** surface: npm scripts, CLI, env vars, API entrypoints, workflows, conventions scoped to that package |
| **`docs/regna-setup.md`**                          | Install & bootstrap steps                     | Commands or prerequisites change                                                                                   |
| **`docs/TECHNICAL-LOG.md`**                        | Dated **decisions** and cross-cutting changes | Architecture, DB/schema/migrations, env contracts, tooling, client↔server contracts                                |

**When you add something usable** (script, env var, CLI wrapper, technical convention, integration pattern): update the **README of the package or area it belongs to** in the same change. Keep it concise and actionable (tables for scripts/env are fine).

**Do not** put how-to prose or script explanations in `TECHNICAL-LOG.md` or Cursor rules—those belong in READMEs. **Do not** duplicate the technical log in READMEs; link to it only when the _why_ matters for context.

If install commands change, **update `regna-setup.md` in the same change** and reference it in a TECHNICAL-LOG entry.

## Monorepo map (pnpm + Turborepo)

| Area                      | Path                                                | Role                                                                                                                                                   |
| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Shared rules & game logic | `packages/engine` → npm name **`@chess/engine`**    | Pure TypeScript/Zod; **no** UI (Vue/Nuxt), **no** Fastify/socket imports. Used by client + server.                                                     |
| Web client                | `apps/client`                                       | **Nuxt 4**, PixiJS, PWA (`@vite-pwa/nuxt`). Depends on `@chess/engine`.                                                                                |
| API & realtime            | `apps/server`                                       | **Fastify**, **Socket.IO**, **Prisma** + **Supabase Postgres**. Depends on `@chess/engine`.                                                            |
| Root                      | `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `turbo.json` | `pnpm dev` / `build` / `typecheck` via Turbo. Root needs `"packageManager": "pnpm@…"` **without** conflicting `devEngines.packageManager` (Turborepo). |

Workspace dependency name **must** match `packages/engine`’s `"name"` field (`@chess/engine`).

## Clean code (practical baseline)

- **Minimize scope:** smallest correct diff; no unrelated refactors in the same change as a bugfix unless necessary.
- **Match existing style:** naming, imports, file layout, error handling level in surrounding code.
- **No speculative abstraction:** avoid tiny one-off helpers and deep inheritance trees; prefer clarity over cleverness.
- **Comments:** only for non-obvious **game rules**, protocol contracts, or integration quirks—not for restating the code.
- **Types:** prefer explicit types at boundaries (API, engine public exports); avoid `any` unless justified and localized.
- **Tests:** add or adjust tests when behavior is non-trivial or regression-prone; skip trivial assertions.

## Git commit messages (Conventional Commits)

- Use **[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)**: `type(scope): short summary` (e.g. `feat(engine): validate card cost on play`, `fix(server): cors preflight on game join`).
- **Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style` (formatting only), `refactor`, `test`, `chore` / `build` / `ci` as appropriate.
- **Subject line:** imperative mood (“add”, “fix”, not “added”); **short** (aim ≤ ~72 chars); state **what matters** for history—intent and user-visible area, not every file touched.
- **Body:** optional; use only when the _why_ is not obvious from the subject (breaking change, migration note, ticket ref). Keep it **brief**—details belong in code and **`docs/TECHNICAL-LOG.md`** when architectural.

## Boundaries agents must respect

- **Engine** stays framework-agnostic: chess/powers/card rules and validators live here; rendering and I/O stay in client/server.
- **Client ↔ server:** document new or changed events/payloads in code and, if architectural, in **`docs/TECHNICAL-LOG.md`**.
- **Secrets:** never commit `.env` or credentials; reference only `env` **names** in docs and the technical log.

## Checklist before finishing a task that touches stack or data

1. Does the **README** for the affected package/area need an update? (new scripts, env, usage, conventions)
2. Does **`docs/TECHNICAL-LOG.md`** need a new entry? (architecture, DB, env contract, tooling, cross-service contract)
3. Does **`docs/regna-setup.md`** need edits? (if install/run steps changed)
4. Do migrations or `schema` changes include a one-line **rollout** note in the log?
